Result is a string representation of a tuple of two SMILES? It shows "(('COc1ccc(C(=O)c2ccc(OC)cc2)cc1', '[Li]C[Si](C)(C)C'),)". So precursor list likely two molecules: "COc1ccc(C(=O)c2ccc(OC)cc2)cc1" and "[Li]C[Si](C)(C)C". The second is a silyl lithium reagent (maybe Me3SiLi). The first is a diaryl ketone with methoxy groups: anisole-CO-anisole (p-anisoyl anisole). So retrosynthesis: target (stilbene) from ketone via Wittig? Actually the template likely is a McMurry coupling (ketone to alkene using TiCl4/Zn). The precursors: a diaryl ketone and a silyl lithium reagent (maybe used for McMurry). But we just need to present route JSON.

We need at least 1 reaction. Use template_id 1679747. Children are precursor molecules.

Thus route JSON:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles":"C=C(C1=CC=C(OC)C=C1)C2=CC=C(OC)C=C2",
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id":1679747,
     "children":[
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"COc1ccc(C(=O)c2ccc(OC)cc2)cc1"},
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"[Li]C[Si](C)(C)C"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

Check if need numeric template_id as int or string? Example uses 1234 (int). We'll use 1679747 as int.

Now verify route schema. Use verify_route.
